  "strategy": "To improve the upper bound of the Erd\u0151s minimum overlap problem constant C\u2085, I will implement an advanced optimization strategy that leverages multiple heuristics and different search directions to avoid local optima. Here's a detailed step-by-step plan:\n\n1. **Initial Strategy**: Use the current construction (initial_h_values) as a starting point but explore variations by perturbing it.\n\n2. **Multistart Optimization**: Run multiple optimization runs with different perturbations of the initial guess. This helps in avoiding local minima and converging to better solutions.\n\n3. **Different Optimization Techniques**:\n   - Combine simulated annealing with local gradient descent.\n   - Use a hybrid approach where early iterations use a global search (e.g., simulated annealing), and later iterations use a local optimization method.\n\n4. **Algorithm Selection**:\n   - Use a combination of global and local search algorithms for robustness.\n   - When using local optimization methods like SLSQP, adjust the tolerance and maximum iterations to find a balance between speed and accuracy.\n\n5. **Diversification of Intermediate Solutions**:\n   - Every few iterations, introduce random perturbations to the current best solution to explore new regions of the solution space.\n   - Use Sobol sequences or Latin hypercube sampling for random perturbations to avoid bias in random number generation.\n\n6. **Adaptively Adjust Search Space**:\n   - If the overlap integral (C\u2085) is not improving over several iterations, adjust the bounds or use a different parametrization of the function h.\n   - Experiment with different types of functions, such as piecewise constant or smooth functions, to better approximate the minimum overlap.\n\n7. **Early Stopping and Budget Management**:\n   - Monitor the time used and ensure the algorithm doesn't exceed the budget.\n   - Stop early if no significant improvements are observed in the last few iterations.\n\n8. **Post-Processing and Verification**:\n   - After finding the best solution, double-check its validity and compute the overlap integral to ensure it meets the constraints.\n   - Cross-validate the result with different initial points and optimization methods to estimate the quality of the solution.\n\n9. **Performance Monitoring**:\n   - Track the best solution and its corresponding C\u2085 value.\n   - Store the best solution at each step to ensure we have a good final result within the time limit.\n\nBy combining these strategies, I aim to find a better solution that results in a lower C\u2085 value and provides a tighter upper bound for the Erd\u0151s constant.",
